@startuml tool_system_architecture
title CampusClaw Built-in Tool System Target Architecture

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/AgentTool.java, AgentTool
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java, ToolExecutionPipeline
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java, AgentSession
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/catalog/ToolCatalog.java, ToolCatalog
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java, AgentRuntimeManager
' Observed behavior: the Java baseline uses a large CLI session, catalog discovery, extension tools, and separate HTTP assembly.
' Architecture change: the target has exactly twelve built-in tools and one lightweight session assembly path.
' Design reason: entry points share execution semantics while hosts retain persistence and lifecycle ownership.

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

package "Hosts" {
  component "CLI Host" as CLI
  component "HTTP Host" as HTTP
  component "Cron Host" as CRON
  component "Child Host" as CHILD
}

package "Common session runtime" {
  component "AgentSessionFactory" as SF
  component "Lightweight AgentSession" as SESSION
  component "ToolExecutionPipeline" as PIPE
  component "Immutable hook chain" as HOOKS
}

package "Built-in tool assembly" {
  component "Strict tool profiles" as PROFILES
  component "ConfiguredToolAssembler" as ASSEMBLER
  component "BuiltInToolFactory" as FACTORY
  component "Fresh tool instances\nper session" as TOOLS
}

package "Shared application dependencies" {
  component "File operations" as OPS
  component "Bash executor" as BASH
  component "FileMutationQueue" as FMQ
  component "MateToolClient" as MATE
  component "Cron services" as CRONSVC
}

package "Managed runtime" {
  component "AgentRuntimeManager" as ARM
  folder "agent/{agentId}/.campusclaw" as DIR
  component "Skill package discovery" as PKG
}

CLI --> SF : create CLI session
HTTP --> SF : create active execution session
CRON --> SF : create scheduled execution session
CHILD --> SF : create child execution session
SF --> SESSION
SESSION --> PIPE
PIPE --> HOOKS
SF --> ASSEMBLER
ASSEMBLER --> PROFILES
ASSEMBLER --> FACTORY
FACTORY --> TOOLS
FACTORY --> OPS
FACTORY --> BASH
FACTORY --> FMQ
FACTORY --> MATE
FACTORY --> CRONSVC
SF --> ARM : prepare managed agent
ARM --> DIR
DIR --> PKG : skills only
DIR --> ASSEMBLER : identity and name indexes

note bottom of PROFILES
BuiltInToolName and ToolEntryPoint
are closed enums.
No dynamic registration or Java Extension SDK.
end note

note bottom of SESSION
Same model, prompt, tools, hooks,
errors, cancellation, and event semantics.
Host persistence is outside this component.
end note
@enduml

@startuml agent_session_assembly
title AgentSession Assembly for Four Entry Points

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/cli/CampusClawCommand.java, createAgentSession
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java, createEngine
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/cron/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/cron/engine/CronJobExecutor.java, execute
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/TransientAgentRunner.java, run
' Observed behavior: each entry point currently assembles or creates its Agent differently.
' Architecture change: one factory creates a fresh lightweight session for all entry points.
' Design reason: common behavior prevents tool, hook, cancellation, and model-policy drift.

skinparam shadowing false
actor "Host" as HOST
collections "Current large CLI AgentSession" as CURRENT
participant "AgentSessionFactory" as SF
participant "AgentRuntimeManager" as ARM
participant "ModelBindingResolver" as MODEL
participant "ConfiguredToolAssembler" as TA
participant "BuiltInToolFactory" as TF
participant "HookChainProvider" as HP
participant "AgentSession" as SESSION

note over HOST
Entry point is one of:
CLI, RUNTIME, CRON, CHILD_AGENT
end note

CURRENT -> HOST : move JSONL, templates, reload, and Loop ownership
CURRENT -> SF : move common assembly
CURRENT -> SESSION : retain only execution semantics

HOST -> SF : create(request, entryPoint)
SF -> ARM : prepare(agentId)
ARM --> SF : immutable managed runtime
SF -> MODEL : resolve allowed model and thinking
MODEL --> SF : execution model snapshot
SF -> TA : assemble(entryPoint, context)
TA -> TA : read strict replacement profile
loop for each configured BuiltInToolName
  TA -> TF : create(name, immutable context)
  TF --> TA : fresh AgentTool instance
end
TA --> SF : ordered immutable tool list
SF -> HP : hooksFor(entryPoint)
HP --> SF : ordered immutable chain
SF -> SESSION : new(model, prompt, tools, hooks, cancellation)
SESSION --> SF : ready
SF --> HOST : fresh session

note over SF,SESSION
The factory does not own JSONL, database state,
CLI reload state, Loop state, or host shutdown.
end note
@enduml

@startuml managed_runtime_refresh
title Managed Runtime Prepare and Explicit Refresh

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java, prepare and materialize
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/session/AgentSession.java, reload
' Observed behavior: prepare is cache-first but currently materializes in place and has no explicit atomic refresh operation.
' Security hardening: target creation and refresh validate a complete sibling tree before atomic publication.
' Design reason: refresh failure must preserve the previous directory and active session.

skinparam shadowing false
actor "Managed CLI" as CLI
participant "AgentRuntimeManager" as ARM
participant "Per-agent lock" as LOCK
participant "MateServiceClient" as MATE
collections "Sibling temp directory" as TEMP
database "Published directory" as LIVE
participant "AgentSessionFactory" as SF

group prepare(agentId)
  CLI -> ARM : prepare(agentId)
  ARM -> LIVE : validate completeness
  alt complete cache exists
    LIVE --> ARM : immutable runtime
    ARM --> CLI : cached runtime
  else missing or incomplete
    ARM -> LOCK : lock(agentId)
    ARM -> MATE : fetch agent, direct skills, direct agents
    MATE --> ARM : remote snapshot
    ARM -> TEMP : write complete managed tree
    ARM -> TEMP : validate names, IDs, versions, and files
    ARM -> LIVE : atomically publish validated tree
    ARM -> LOCK : unlock
    ARM --> CLI : prepared runtime
  end
end

group explicit refresh from /reload
  CLI -> ARM : refresh(agentId)
  ARM -> LOCK : lock(agentId)
  ARM -> MATE : fetch fresh remote snapshot
  MATE --> ARM : remote snapshot
  ARM -> TEMP : build and validate replacement
  alt replacement valid
    ARM -> LIVE : atomic replace
    ARM -> LOCK : unlock
    ARM --> CLI : refreshed runtime
    CLI -> SF : rebuild lightweight session
    SF --> CLI : new session
    alt current model remains usable
      CLI -> CLI : preserve model and thinking
    else new default model is usable
      CLI -> CLI : switch model and notify user
    else no usable default
      CLI -> LIVE : restore previous published tree
      CLI -> CLI : keep old session
    end
  else fetch, build, or validation fails
    ARM -> LOCK : unlock
    ARM --> CLI : refresh error
    CLI -> CLI : keep old directory and session
  end
end

note over CLI,SF
Messages, thinking, and SessionLoopController survive reload.
Application tool profiles are not reloaded.
end note
@enduml

@startuml list_mate_tools_sequence
title ListMateTools Live Discovery

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/mate/ListMateTool.java, execute
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java, listTools and queryToolMetaByIds
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentRuntimeManager.java, materialized skill identity gap
' Observed behavior: the baseline accepts agent_id or skill_id and returns formatted text.
' Architecture change: target input accepts only optional skillName and output is stable JSON without internal IDs.
' Design reason: local name indexes preserve usability while Mate remains the live authorization and metadata source.

skinparam shadowing false
actor "Model" as MODEL
participant "ListMateTools" as TOOL
collections "Managed name indexes" as INDEX
participant "MateToolClient" as CLIENT
participant "Binding API" as BINDING
participant "Tool metadata batch API" as META

MODEL -> TOOL : {skillName?}
alt skillName absent
  TOOL -> CLIENT : listAgentTools(currentAgentId)
  CLIENT -> BINDING : query agent binding tool IDs
else skillName present
  TOOL -> INDEX : resolve exact skill name
  INDEX --> TOOL : skillId or error
  TOOL -> CLIENT : listSkillTools(skillId)
  CLIENT -> BINDING : query skill binding tool IDs
end
BINDING --> CLIENT : ordered internal tool IDs
alt no bindings
  CLIENT --> TOOL : empty list
else bindings exist
  CLIENT -> META : batch query metadata by IDs
  META --> CLIENT : unordered metadata records
  CLIENT -> CLIENT : join by ID and restore binding order
  CLIENT --> TOOL : internal metadata list
end
TOOL -> TOOL : project scope and tools
TOOL --> MODEL : stable JSON

note over TOOL,MODEL
Visible fields per item:
name, description, inputSchema

Hidden fields:
IDs, permission, outputSchema,
and concurrency metadata
end note

note over TOOL,CLIENT
Every invocation performs a live query.
No list cache and no mandatory list-before-call state.
end note
@enduml

@startuml subagent_execution_sequence
title Bound Child Agent Execution

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/AgentBindingResolver.java, resolve and validate
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtime/TransientAgentRunner.java, run
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/tool/delegation/InvokeAgentTool.java, execute
' Source evidence: pi-mono packages/coding-agent/examples/extensions/subagent/index.ts, runSingleAgent
' Source evidence: opencode packages/opencode/src/tool/task.ts, TaskTool
' Observed behavior: Java uses after-hook delegation and placeholder authorization; pi demonstrates subprocess isolation; OpenCode creates a child session.
' Architecture change: target uses a first-class Agent tool and in-JVM isolated child session.
' Product constraint: only directly bound child names are callable and maximum depth defaults to one.

skinparam shadowing false
actor "Parent model" as MODEL
participant "BoundAgentTool" as TOOL
participant "AgentBindingResolver" as RESOLVER
participant "AgentRuntimeManager" as ARM
participant "SubagentExecutionService" as SERVICE
participant "OneShotSubagentRunner" as RUNNER
participant "AgentSessionFactory" as SF
participant "Child AgentSession" as CHILD

MODEL -> TOOL : Agent({agentName, task})
TOOL -> RESOLVER : resolve exact direct binding
RESOLVER -> RESOLVER : check enabled and fixed version
RESOLVER -> RESOLVER : check depth and ancestry cycle
alt validation fails
  RESOLVER --> TOOL : rejection
  TOOL --> MODEL : text result, isError=true
else binding valid
  RESOLVER --> TOOL : bound child identity
  TOOL -> SERVICE : execute(context, child, task)
  SERVICE -> ARM : prepare(childAgentId)
  ARM --> SERVICE : child managed runtime
  SERVICE -> RUNNER : run isolated execution
  RUNNER -> SF : create CHILD_AGENT session
  SF --> RUNNER : fresh child session
  RUNNER -> CHILD : prompt(task)
  CHILD --> RUNNER : high-level progress events
  RUNNER --> SERVICE : final assistant text
  SERVICE --> TOOL : execution result
  TOOL --> MODEL : final child text
end

note over SERVICE,CHILD
Child cwd, prompt, skills, messages, and tools are isolated.
Parent cancellation propagates to the child.
No reasoning or child history is returned.
end note
@enduml

@startuml tool_batch_scheduling
title Per-tool Batch Scheduling with Sequential Barriers

' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionPipeline.java, executeAll
' Source evidence: pi-mono-java modules/agent-core/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/agent/tool/ToolExecutionMode.java, ToolExecutionMode
' Observed behavior: the Java baseline applies one execution mode to the complete batch and validates after the before hook.
' Architecture change: target mode is declared per AgentTool and schema validation occurs before hooks.
' Design reason: read-only calls can overlap without allowing state-changing tools to cross a barrier.

skinparam shadowing false
actor "Agent loop" as LOOP
participant "Batch planner" as PLAN
participant "Virtual-thread executor" as VTE
participant "Tool pipeline" as PIPE
collections "Ordered results" as RESULTS

LOOP -> PLAN : ordered calls [P1, P2, S3, P4, P5, S6]
PLAN -> PLAN : partition adjacent PARALLEL runs

group parallel run P1, P2
  PLAN -> VTE : submit P1 and P2
  VTE -> PIPE : validate schema, before, execute, after, event
  VTE -> PIPE : validate schema, before, execute, after, event
  VTE --> PLAN : join both
  PLAN -> RESULTS : append P1 then P2
end

group sequential barrier S3
  PLAN -> PIPE : validate schema, before, execute, after, event
  PIPE --> PLAN : S3 result
  PLAN -> RESULTS : append S3
end

group parallel run P4, P5
  PLAN -> VTE : submit P4 and P5
  VTE -> PIPE : execute each call independently
  VTE --> PLAN : join both
  PLAN -> RESULTS : append P4 then P5
end

group sequential barrier S6
  PLAN -> PIPE : execute S6
  PIPE --> PLAN : S6 result
  PLAN -> RESULTS : append S6
end

RESULTS --> LOOP : [R1, R2, R3, R4, R5, R6]

note over PLAN,PIPE
Default executionMode is SEQUENTIAL.
Handlers must be thread-safe.
Failures become text results with isError=true.
end note
@enduml
